                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239521809",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198201620245",
                            "num_reviews": 724,
                            "playtime_forever": 298,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 298,
                            "last_played": 1790422259
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You play as a chameleon who controls his emotions so perfectly that he can change his mood/colour at will to match the carpets, thus becoming invisible on them.\nEither that, or it's a defective shellfish that can't mimic floor patterns, only flat colours, and disguises itself as a reptile for reasons unknown.\n\nThe gameplay is simple and rather nervous, mostly entertaining; the visuals, a tad ugly but serviceable; the level design, unpolished, doesn't bring a progressive raise in challenge.\nIndeed. said challenge generally remains low, but with the occasional, randomly situated spike in difficulty, always due to very narrow windows for your timed moves.\nSome of them feel like they require more luck than skill.\n\nI'm dropping out on one such spike, but I still raise the critical thumb: it's not a bad game, and its abundant checkpoints make it completable, with just a bit more patience and repetition that I'm willing to give to the precision running genre.",
